==================================================

Files Modified:
- README.md: Added "Verbosity Control" subsection under CLI Command Summary
  with flag table, examples, and "always shown" note.
- docs/USER_GUIDE.md: Added section 3.11 "Global Verbosity Flags" with:
  - Usage syntax
  - Flag table (--verbose/-v, --quiet/-q)
  - Verbose mode section with examples and sample output
  - Quiet mode section with CI examples and sample output
  - Mutual exclusion section with error example
  - Exit codes table

Content covers:
- Verbose: shows underlying commands (Godot/GUT, gdlint, gdformat) and timing
- Quiet: suppresses update checks, info messages, init/doctor details
- Always shown: test summaries, lint violations, coverage, errors, exit codes
- Mutual exclusion: --verbose --quiet exits 2
- Default: no visible change to output
